/* Glyphs. Every value comes from the element the glyph sits in; nothing here is
   a literal colour and nothing here is a token, because a drawn glyph has no
   colour and no size of its own. */

/* `1em` square, so the size comes from the `font-size` the glyph element already
   sets from `--gs-size-icon-control` or `--gs-size-icon-hero`. That is how the
   emoji these replace were sized, so no call site changed its CSS.

   `inline-block` rather than `block`, for the same reason: the emoji was inline
   content of its span, and a block would drop the label under it wherever a
   glyph and a word share a line. `vertical-align: middle` puts the drawing where
   the character used to sit on the baseline. */
.gs-glyph {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 1em;
  height: 1em;
  vertical-align: middle;
}
